	"title"		"BrainFog / 脑雾尖塔"
	"description"		"[h1]脑雾尖塔 BrainFog[/h1]

大部分尖塔文字将被替换为乱码，可在内置修改器中使部分游戏内容恢复正常。

[h2]0.4.0 更新（2026-11-14）[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]同步 STS2 v0.113.0 测试版[/b]：支持 [b]Blitz（闪电）[/b] 与 [b]Dread（恐惧）[/b] 新模式；新角色「愚者」的卡牌走通用卡面/文字规则。
[*][b]Blitz[/b]：没有幕地图与金币；地图迷雾和「显示地图所有路线」在该模式自动跳过，金币界面保持原版。
[*][b]Dread[/b]：全飞升词缀、支配与诅咒照常生效；新获得的诅咒先认得，之后仍受记忆规则影响。
[*][b]联机「只盲自己」[/b]：多人对局不再自动禁用。每个玩家只影响自己的卡牌与记忆；队友卡牌/召唤物保持原版；「记忆消逝」联机停用；好友联机无需安装同版本 BrainFog。
[*]版本窗口：[b]v0.107.1 – v0.113.0[/b]。
[/list]

[h2]认知修改器[/h2]
主标题界面与对局内均可操作（可拖动/收起/缩进屏幕边缘；「当前设置为默认」保存自己的默认，「重置为默认」一键恢复）：
[list]
[*][b]总开关[/b]：「关闭脑雾尖塔」一键停用本 mod（不再影响游戏），取消勾选即恢复
[*][b]文字[/b]：乱码百分比 0%–100% 自由调节；乱码模式：固定混乱（重进不变）/ 混乱混乱（每次重进重新随机）
[*][b]认知[/b]：卡牌奖励揭示（不揭示 / 随机揭示1-3张 / 奖励全部揭示）；商店与事件卡面揭示开关；卡牌记忆四模式；记忆消逝开关
[*][b]感知[/b]：血量/金币失忆模式；血量数/金币数恢复正常显示；显示遗物（全场景恢复：已拥有/奖励/商店/宝箱/检视/跑图历史）；显示地图所有路线（含阶段 Boss 图标与图例恢复；其悬停描述仍随乱码百分比）；敌人模型可见；敌人意图（不可见 / 仅第一回合 / 全部可见）
[/list]

默认配置偏辅助：卡牌奖励全部揭示、商店/事件卡面揭示、血量/金币数值可读、遗物可见、地图全路线、敌人模型与敌人意图可见；可逐项恢复难度，并用「当前设置为默认」保存自己的默认。

[h2]卡牌记忆四模式[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]通晓万物[/b]：全部卡牌直接可见
[*][b]好记性[/b]：打出/升级一次即永久记住，同名卡在所有奖励/商店/事件中也显示真牌面
[*][b]坏记性[/b]（默认）：每张卡上手 n 次未打出就会忘记（n 默认 2、可调）；打出重置计数；新获得的牌先认得，即将失忆的手牌会变暗提醒
[*][b]歪比巴卜[/b]：卡牌永不揭示
[/list]

开局牌组视为记得（好记性/坏记性）。[b]记忆消逝[/b]（开关，默认开）：战斗结束时仍未揭示的牌会从卡组中移除，并播放原版删卡动画（歪比巴卜模式不受影响，无保底）。联机下该规则自动停用（会改写共享卡组状态），其余功能只影响你自己。

[h2]核心效果[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]卡牌失认[/b]：开局牌组视为记得；默认打过的牌才认得；奖励与选牌界面默认全部揭示（可调回仅显示稀有度）
[*][b]文字失读[/b]：事件、菜单、提示、卡面与对话全部乱码（图鉴与设置除外），乱码程度可调
[*][b]记忆失真[/b]：血量与金币默认实时且数值可读；可切换失忆模式停留在「上次休息时」，或关闭「血量数/金币数恢复正常显示」让数值重新乱码
[*][b]世界模糊[/b]：敌人默认显示真实模型（可关闭恢复呼吸方框）、名字隐藏；遗物默认可见（可关闭「显示遗物」恢复遮蔽）、药水只剩轮廓、地图迷雾、Boss 信息隐藏；受击/治疗数字乱码
[/list]

支持 STS2 v0.107.1–v0.113.0（正式服/测试服，含 Blitz/Dread 新模式）与 RitsuLib 0.6.2；单人完整，联机只影响自己；卸载即恢复原版。

Github链接：https://github.com/yM7-1/BrainFog

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BrainFog[/h1]

Most text in the Spire is replaced with garbled static — use the built-in modifier to restore parts of the game.

[h2]0.4.0 Update (2026-11-14)[/h2]
[list]
[*]Synced with STS2 v0.113.0 beta: Blitz/Dread modes and The Fool (generic card rules).
[*]Blitz skips map fog and map/gold options; Dread curses and dominions follow the usual memory rules.
[*]Co-op is local-only: teammates stay vanilla, memory fade is disabled, and friends do not need the same BrainFog version.
[*]Supported window: v0.107.1 – v0.113.0.
[/list]

[h2]Cognition Modifier[/h2]
Available on the main menu and in-run (draggable, collapsible, dockable; Set current as default saves your defaults, Reset to defaults restores them):
[list]
[*][b]Kill switch[/b]: Disable BrainFog turns the whole mod off (no effect on the game); uncheck to re-enable it
[*][b]Text[/b]: unified blur percentage 0%–100%; blur mode: fixed chaos / re-rolled on every launch
[*][b]Cognition[/b]: card reward reveal (none / random 1-3 / all); shop & event card faces on/off; four card-memory modes; memory fade
[*][b]Perception[/b]: HP/gold amnesia mode; readable HP/gold numbers; show relics (all contexts: owned/rewards/shops/chests/inspect/history); show all map routes (restores the act-boss icon and the legend; their hover descriptions still follow the text blur); visible enemy models; enemy intents (hidden / first round only / always)
[/list]

The default preset is lenient: all reward cards revealed, shop/event card faces revealed, readable HP/gold numbers, relics visible, all map routes, enemy models and intents visible. Tone the difficulty back up per option, or save your own defaults with Set current as default.

[h2]Card memory modes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Omniscience[/b]: every card is visible
[*][b]Good memory[/b]: playing/upgrading a card remembers it for the run — including its copies in rewards, shops and events
[*][b]Bad memory[/b] (default): a card is forgotten after n unplayed draws (n defaults to 2, adjustable); playing resets the counter; newly acquired cards start known, and a hand card about to be forgotten dims
[*][b]Nonsense[/b]: cards are never revealed
[/list]

The starting deck counts as known (good/bad memory). [b]Memory fade[/b] (on by default): cards still unrevealed at the end of a combat are removed from the deck with the original removal animation (nonsense mode exempt; no floor). In co-op this rule is automatically disabled (it would write shared deck state); everything else only affects you.

[h2]Core effects[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Card agnosia[/b]: the starting deck is remembered; by default only cards you have played are recognized; rewards/selection are fully revealed by default (can be set back to rarity only)
[*][b]Text alexia[/b]: events, menus, prompts, card text and dialogue are garbled (compendium and settings stay readable); the level is adjustable
[*][b]Faulty memory[/b]: HP and gold are live and readable by default; switch on amnesia mode to freeze them at your last rest, or turn readable HP/gold numbers off to garble them again
[*][b]Blurred world[/b]: enemies show their real models by default (turn visible enemy models off to restore the breathing boxes), names stay hidden; relics visible by default (turn Show relics off to mask them again), potions outlined, map fogged, boss info hidden; damage/heal numbers garbled
[/list]

Supports STS2 v0.107.1–v0.113.0 (stable/beta, including Blitz/Dread) + RitsuLib 0.6.2. Single-player fully supported; in co-op BrainFog only affects you; uninstall restores everything.

GitHub: https://github.com/yM7-1/BrainFog"
